From: garrick247 <garrick.wagner@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] typecheck: propagate body assume/assert facts to postcondition check

stmt_final_env's SExpr branch had handlers for EAssign/EIf/ECall but no
case for EAssume/EAssert, so its catch-all fell through to expr_final_env
which returns env unchanged. The result: in-body `assume(pred)` and
`assert(pred)` statements were silently dropped from the body_env used
in the function's postcondition check.

Meanwhile check_stmt's SExpr handler (line 2828) correctly calls
env_add_fact env pred for both EAssume and EAssert, with the comment
"add to context so downstream proofs can use it." The two code paths
processed the same statement type with different semantics.

Symptom: any function with `ensures P` where the body proves P via an
explicit `assume(...)` (e.g. trusted Montgomery analysis bounds in
proven-elsewhere chains) reports proof_failed even when the assume's
predicate would imply P trivially. SMT dump shows the assume's
predicate literally absent from the Z3 query.

Reproduction:

  fn test_assume(x: u32) -> u32
      ensures result == 42u32
  {
      assume(x == 100u32) "test";
      x + 0u32 - 58u32
  }

  // Pre-fix: proof_failed (need: ((x + 0) - 58) == 42, no assume in env)
  // Post-fix: proof_ok, audit log: 1 assumption

Fix: add explicit EAssume/EAssert cases to stmt_final_env's SExpr branch,
mirroring check_stmt's existing behavior. The assume audit-log mechanism
is preserved — every assumption is still tracked for review. Security
model unchanged.

Discovered while building math-correctness specs for the Stark prime in
demos/std/felt252.fg. The v2 Montgomery reduce chain composition needed
~12 audited assumes for Montgomery analysis bounds; pre-fix none of them
reached Z3 and the postcondition couldn't be derived from the otherwise-
proven case-split asserts.

Tested: 27_induction.fg, 31_lemma_postcond.fg, 22_proof_terms.fg, and
the full demos/std/felt252.fg (10,215 lines, 3030/3030 SMT obligations
discharged with 12 audit assumptions) all verify post-fix.

---
 lib/types/typecheck.ml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/types/typecheck.ml b/lib/types/typecheck.ml
index aaaaaaa..bbbbbbb 100644
--- a/lib/types/typecheck.ml
+++ b/lib/types/typecheck.ml
@@ -1327,6 +1327,8 @@
       env_assign_var env name (expr_to_pred_simple rhs)
   | SExpr e ->
       (match e.expr_desc with
+       | EAssume (pred, _) -> env_add_fact env pred
+       | EAssert (pred, _) -> env_add_fact env pred
        | EAssign (lhs, rhs) ->
            (match lhs.expr_desc with
             | EVar v ->
